From: FTTR maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: drain hardware flows before removing block callbacks

Direct ndo_setup_tc callbacks are removed before nf_flow_table_free() tears
down the flows. On Airoha this leaves PPE entries forwarding after a fw4
reload, with no software flow remaining to revoke them on policy changes.

Drain outstanding work and tear down the table while the callbacks are
still installed. Drain the whole table: a detached device can be an
egress device, or a physical lower device absent from the logical ingress
ifindices stored in bridge tuples. Remaining devices can admit new flows
after the detach operation completes.

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
@@ -1282,6 +1282,15 @@ int nf_flow_table_offload_setup(struct nf
 	if (!nf_flowtable_hw_offload(flowtable))
 		return nf_flow_offload_xdp_setup(flowtable, dev, cmd);
 
+	/* Destroy rules before ndo_setup_tc removes their block callbacks.
+	 * Device-only ingress cleanup misses egress and lower-device rules.
+	 * Finish queued installs before collecting flows for teardown.
+	 */
+	if (cmd == FLOW_BLOCK_UNBIND) {
+		nf_flow_table_offload_flush(flowtable);
+		nf_flow_table_gc_cleanup(flowtable, NULL);
+	}
+
 	if (dev->netdev_ops->ndo_setup_tc)
 		err = nf_flow_table_offload_cmd(&bo, flowtable, dev, cmd,
 						&extack);
